What is Utility Circular Economy?
Utility Circular Economy is a systemic approach that re‑engineers traditional utility infrastructure to treat waste streams as valuable inputs rather than disposal endpoints. It integrates resource recovery (e.g., reclaimed water, biogas, secondary metals), product‑as‑a‑service models, and digital platforms that enable real‑time material flow tracking. The concept aligns economic performance with environmental stewardship by turning cost centers into revenue‑generating assets.
